  "body": "The base is now `main`.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- `stock_sim::breaks::breaks_stock_edge` now includes a Deburr whose source is the setup's stock. The program sim gives its bevel no edge-break credit (#303) over a part's columns.\r\n- `keep_law::is_stock_kept_kind` now includes Deburr. At generation the solid law keeps the cut out of each part of the setup. The post's live re-judge names a part that is added after generation.\r\n- New function `stock_sim::breaks::stock_part_of`. It finds a from-model stock whose facets equal a judged part in place (vertex for vertex, 1e-6). That stock IS the part. A Deburr off that stock keeps the credit, and `parts_in_stock` / `kept_models` spare that one part. All other parts stay kept.\r\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2313-stock-deburr-credit.md`.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/stock_deburr_part.rs`)\r\n\r\n- `a_stock_source_deburr_into_a_part_known_at_generation_never_posts`: about 1 mm into \"other\", on aligned stock and on stock turned a quarter about Z. The op has a blocking gouge, and the post refuses with the sim's gouge line.\r\n- `a_part_added_under_a_stock_source_deburr_is_refused_by_name`: 1 mm and 0.05 mm, aligned and quarter turn. The setup posts before the part is added. After that, the post refuses with \"S1 now cuts part 'other'\".\r\n- `a_stock_source_deburr_clear_of_every_part_still_posts`: aligned and quarter turn.\r\n- `a_deburr_of_the_parts_own_edge_still_posts`: a part source, and a stock source on a from-model stock.\r\n\r\n## Mutations\r\n\r\n- All `src` changes reverted: the first two tests fail (no gouge at generation; the setup posts after the part is added).\r\n- `stock_part_of` forced to `None`: only `a_deburr_of_the_parts_own_edge_still_posts` fails. The from-model exemption carries load.\r\n\r\n## Readings (debug, `-p camcraft-app`, `--test-threads=6`)\r\n\r\nAll pass:\r\n- `stock_deburr_part` 4\r\n- `stock_chamfer_added_part` 3\r\n- `edge_break_gate` 5\r\n- `edge_break_bound` 5\r\n- `stock_source_holes` 9\r\n- `keep_law` 31\r\n- `kept_parts_live` 4\r\n- `post_not_judged` 4\r\n- `golden_cl` 33\r\n- `deburr_links` 1\r\n- `edge_volume_bound` 2\r\n- `setup_carry_credits` 7\r\n- `setup_align_2d_kinds` 8\r\n- `stock_source_cross_drill` 6\r\n- `operations` filtered to `deburr`: 5\r\n\r\n`cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- For a part known at generation, the post line does not name the part. The refusal is the sim's located gouge plus the op's own blocking gouge finding.\r\n- A stock that the sim cannot judge (an odd turn): only the live re-judge acts. No test covers it here.\r\n- This change is stricter in one case. A stock-source Deburr on a box stock, or on a from-model stock moved off its source, now takes the solid law. If its cone reaches a part, the result is a gouge. The workaround is a part source. No existing test had this case.\r\n- No full suite run and no GUI run.\r\n\r\n## Review fix (head after 820245b9b)\r\n\r\n- New finding `Warning::StockDeburrGouge` (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`). Text: `move N cuts past the finish surface (stock-source deburr breaks into a part; use the part as source)`. `keep_law::note_stock_chamfer_gouges` writes it for a stock-source Deburr. MCP reports it as `gouge`.\r\n- When the sim gouge verdict blocks the post, the post line now also names the convicted op and the part (`posting_sim::stock_edge_named`, `kept_rejudge::stock_edge_problem`): `... - S1 breaks into part 'other' (move N cuts past the finish surface (stock-source deburr breaks into a part; use the part as source))`.\r\n- The live re-judge of a part added after generation says the Deburr way out.\r\n- New pin `a_from_model_stock_moved_off_its_part_is_not_the_part`: a from-model stock moved 0.5 mm in X, aligned and turned a quarter about Z. The stock-source Deburr is refused.\r\n- `a_stock_source_deburr_into_a_part_known_at_generation_never_posts` now asserts the op name, the part name and the way out in the post line.\r\n- Mutation: `stock_part_of` without the facet check makes the new pin fail. Mutation: no `stock_edge_named` makes the known-part pin and the new pin fail.\r\n- Readings: `stock_deburr_part` 5, `stock_chamfer_added_part` 3, `keep_law` 31, `kept_parts_live` 4, `edge_break_gate` 5, `post_not_judged` 4, `stock_source_holes` 9, `camcraft-sim` lib 184: all pass. Clippy `-p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets` and `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets`, `-D warnings`: clean.\r\n- Not exercised: a raw-stock-only or fixture source for the from-model exception (the code refuses the exception there; no test).\r\n\r\nChangelog: A Deburr with the stock as its source that cuts into a part is now refused at the post and names the operation and the part; a Deburr on a from-model stock that is the part still posts.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nFixes #2313\r\n\r\n\r\n",
